response.text:
{
  "layperson_summary": "This extension is designed to manage your browser cookies and has access to read and change cookies for every website you visit. However, it contains hidden code that secretly sends your cookies to an external server. The most important thing to weigh is that this extension can steal your login details for any site you are logged into.",
  "technical_summary": "The extension operates as a cookie manager with broad access, utilizing the `cookies` permission across `<all_urls>` (finding 3). The background service worker handles cookie CRUD operations and context menus (finding 2). A critical behavior was verified where `js/_locale_pack.js` uses an obfuscated string decoder to build a URL and exfiltrates `document.cookie` via a `fetch()` call (finding 1). Other observed capabilities include an `eval()` call in a bundled jQuery library (finding 4) and navigation to a demo domain (finding 5).",
  "description_deviation": {
    "deviates": true,
    "note": "The extension performs cookie management as stated, but it also contains obfuscated code that exfiltrates cookies to an external server (finding 1), which is a material deviation from its stated purpose."
  }
}
